---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base>
  <section class="section" style="padding-top:84px">
    <div class="wrap" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1.15fr 1fr;gap:48px;align-items:center">
      <div>
        <p class="kicker">The fair-pay cleaning notice board · UK</p>
        <h1>A cleaner who's treated well cleans well.</h1>
        <p style="font-size:1.15rem;color:var(--ink-600);max-width:34em">
          CanYouDo? is a digital notice board that introduces you to independent local cleaners.
          They set their own rates and keep every penny of them. We add a clear service charge on
          top, shown to you upfront — never taken out of their pocket.
        </p>
        <p style="display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:26px">
          <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/find-a-cleaner/">Find a cleaner</a>
          <a class="btn btn-secondary" href="/signup/?role=cleaner">Offer your services</a>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3 style="margin-bottom:14px">How the money works</h3>
          <div class="price-split" role="img" aria-label="The provider's own hourly rate, plus a platform service charge on top">
            <div class="part worker"><span class="amount">Their rate</span><span class="who">set by the cleaner, paid to them in full</span></div>
            <div class="part platform"><span class="amount">+ 20%</span><span class="who">our service charge</span></div>
          </div>
          <p class="hint" style="margin-top:14px">
            Every cleaner publishes their own hourly rate. We add a 20% service charge on top,
            which you see before you book — it covers the booking system, messaging, reviews and
            support. Two separate payments, no hidden cut of their earnings.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-green">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">Why it works</p>
      <h2>Most platforms squeeze the worker.<br />We built one that backs them.</h2>
      <div class="grid-3" style="margin-top:34px">
        <div>
          <h3 style="color:#fff">💷 Their rate, their money</h3>
          <p>Cleaners name their own hourly rate and are paid it directly and in full. Our charge sits on top, visible to the customer — we never take a commission out of what they earn.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 style="color:#fff">📏 Ratings that mean something</h3>
          <p>Reviews cover the things that matter: were they on time, did they clean what was asked, did they follow instructions. Consistent quality earns a higher grading, from New all the way to Superstar.</p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 style="color:#fff">🗓️ Work that fits real life</h3>
          <p>Cleaners set their availability and block out holidays. Customers post the days they want covered — regular slots or one-offs — and cleaners pick up what suits them.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="kicker">Simple by design</p>
      <h2>How it works</h2>
      <div class="grid-3" style="margin-top:30px">
        <div class="card">
          <span class="badge badge-amber">Step 1</span>
          <h3 style="margin-top:12px">Browse or post</h3>
          <p>Search local cleaners by area, day and grading — or post what you need on the board (a regular weekly slot, a one-off, or something urgent) and let cleaners come to you.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="badge badge-amber">Step 2</span>
          <h3 style="margin-top:12px">Agree the details</h3>
          <p>Message through the site to settle access, products and anything specific — including insurance arrangements, which are for the two of you to agree directly.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <span class="badge badge-amber">Step 3</span>
          <h3 style="margin-top:12px">Pay in two parts</h3>
          <p>You pay our service charge online when you book, and pay your cleaner their own rate directly. Afterwards, leave a review — it builds their grading and helps everyone else.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:26px"><a href="/how-it-works/">See the full details →</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="card" style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr auto;gap:20px;align-items:center">
        <div>
          <h2 style="font-size:1.4rem">Cleaners: set your rate, keep it all</h2>
          <p style="margin:0;color:var(--ink-600)">Publish your own hourly rate, control your calendar, block out holidays, add photos of your work, and build a grading that speaks for itself. You stay independent — we just carry the notice board.</p>
        </div>
        <a class="btn btn-amber" href="/signup/?role=cleaner">Join as a provider</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section-tight" style="padding-bottom:70px">
    <div class="wrap-narrow" style="text-align:center">
      <p class="hint">CanYouDo? is a digital notice board that introduces independent cleaners to customers. We are not a cleaning company, employer or agency, and we do not provide or arrange insurance. Cleaners carry their own independent insurance, and insurance arrangements are a matter for the cleaner and customer to discuss and agree directly. <a href="/terms/">Read our terms</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .section .wrap[style*="grid-template-columns"] { grid-template-columns: 1fr !important; }
    .card[style*="grid-template-columns"] { grid-template-columns: 1fr !important; }
  }
</style>
